<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">9 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 9 April, from 193 to 2003.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/septimius-severus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/septimius-severus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">193 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,833 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Danube legions proclaim Septimius Severus emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After the murder of Pertinax, the legions at Carnuntum hailed their governor Septimius Severus as emperor. He marched on Rome, defeated his rivals and founded the Severan dynasty.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septimius-severus">Septimius Severus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1241 CE <span class="tih-ago">785 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mongols defeat a Polish and German army at Legnica</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Mongol force under Baidar and Kadan crushed the army of Duke Henry II the Pious, who was killed. Two days later the main Mongol army destroyed the Hungarians at Mohi.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1682 CE <span class="tih-ago">344 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">La Salle claims the Mississippi basin for France</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Reaching the mouth of the Mississippi, René-Robert Cavelier de La Salle claimed its whole drainage basin for Louis XIV and named it Louisiana. France sold the territory to the United States in 1803.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1865 CE <span class="tih-ago">161 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lee surrenders to Grant at Appomattox Court House</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Robert E. Lee surrendered the Army of Northern Virginia to Ulysses S. Grant. Other Confederate forces followed in the weeks after, bringing the American Civil War to an end.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1940 CE <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany invades Denmark and Norway</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">German forces struck both neutral states in Operation Weserübung. Denmark yielded within hours, while Norway, aided by Britain and France, fought on for two months, giving Germany vital North Sea and Atlantic bases.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1945 CE <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Dietrich Bonhoeffer is executed at Flossenbürg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Lutheran pastor and theologian Dietrich Bonhoeffer was hanged on Hitler's orders for his links to the resistance. He died a month before Germany's surrender.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2003 CE <span class="tih-ago">23 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Baghdad falls and Saddam's statue is pulled down</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">As US troops entered central Baghdad, a statue of Saddam Hussein in Firdos Square was toppled with the help of a Marine vehicle. The images marked the regime's collapse, though years of insurgency followed.</p></div></li></ol>
